    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0565" n="441" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg441"/>

                <head>No. 273.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Evarts to Mr. Outrey</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-03-07"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 7,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have had the honor to receive your note
                    of this day’s date, in which you inform me that the minister of foreign affairs
                    of France has renewed to you the declarations made by his predecessors, and has
                    authorized you to affirm once more the unchangeable resolution of the French
                    Government to maintain the absolutely private and international character of the
                    enterprise of Monsieur de Lesseps.</p>
                <p>Thanking you for these renewed assurances, I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>WM. M. EVARTS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
